    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0250" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg144"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Egan</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-07-09"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 115.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    Nos. 151 and 152, of April 6 and 14 last, relative to a decree of the Chilean
                    Government closing to commerce certain ports of Chile while in the hands of the
                    insurgents.</p>
                <p>In view of the fact that you have “obtained full and friendly assurances that
                    American vessels will not be subjected to any inconveniences,” the necessity for
                    any formal instructions to you in the premises has been anticipated.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
